# L §6.1: "Any other unit a member declares is its own (a.hour)", and L §3.2 adds only quantities of one unit
# (LOAD-UNIT): a.h is in a.hour, b.h in b.hour, two units.
=== joint.tally
model family
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use a = "a.tally" sha256 "44caa3b76989672d221a267a273bfc71bbb8aa4d2e1e066a3252ca68ff56ac8e"
  use b = "b.tally" sha256 "92e909f53a6ef3abdbafe20366fa3ec1a30a18055555ef1752f253727101d9b3"

ask r: a.h + b.h
=== a.tally
model a
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"

unit hour "godzina"

input h: num hour

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  h = 3 hour "umowa"

ask q: h
=== b.tally
model b
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"

unit hour "godzina"

input h: num hour

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  h = 5 hour "umowa"

ask q: h
=== expect
refused: LOAD-UNIT ...
